  "segments": [
    {
      "id": "s0001",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "Name",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0002",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "vfs_streams_xattr — Store alternate data streams in posix xattrs",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0003",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "Synopsis",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0004",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "code",
            "text": "vfs objects = streams_xattr"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0005",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "DESCRIPTION",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0006",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "This VFS module is part of the [[p0]] suite.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "link",
            "text": "samba(7)",
            "href": "https://www.samba.org/samba/docs/current/man-html/samba.7.html"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0007",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "The [[p0]] enables storing of NTFS alternate data streams in the file system. As a normal posix file system does not support the concept of multiple data streams per file, the streams_xattr module stores the data in posix extended attributes (xattrs). The name of these attributes by default is user.DosStream.\"ADS-NAME\". The prefix \"user.DosStream.\" can be changed with the module option [[p1]], but be aware that this will also expose those ADS over the SMB extended attributes interface.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "code",
            "text": "vfs_streams_xattr"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "code",
            "text": "streams_xattr:prefix"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0008",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "The file system that is shared with this module enabled must support xattrs.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0009",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Please note that most file systems have severe limitations on the size of xattrs. So this module might work for applications like IE that stores small zone information in streams but will fail for applications that store serious amounts of data in ADSs.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0010",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "OPTIONS",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0011",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "streams_xattr:prefix = STRING",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0012",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Name prefix used when storing an ADS in an xattr, defaults to [[p0]]. Changing this will also expose ADS over the SMB extended attributes interface.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "code",
            "text": "user.DosStream."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0013",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "streams_xattr:store_stream_type = [yes|no]",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0014",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Whether the xattr names for Alternate Data Streams of type \"$DATA\" are suffixed by the stream type string \":$DATA\". The default is [[p0]].",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "code",
            "text": "yes"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0015",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "streams_xattr:max xattrs per stream = NUM",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0016",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "On file systems where the size of a single xattr is more limited than the overall size of xattrs per inode, setting this parameter to a number between 2 and 16 will allow smbd to store larger streams than what fits into a single xattr. For example Linux has a limit of 64kB per xattr, but XFS can store more than that per inode.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0017",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "The size of a single xattr is limited by the smb.conf parameter [[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "code",
            "text": "smbd max xattr size"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0018",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "This is limited to 16 xattrs per alternate data stream.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0019",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "The default value is [[p0]], compatible to the default behaviour before this feature was introduced.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "code",
            "text": "1"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0020",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "streams_xattr:ext_prefix = STRING",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0021",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Name prefix used when storing overflow xattrs of a stream. It defaults to [[p0]] with the string \"Ext\" appended. If [[p1]] ends in a \".\", \"Ext\" is inserted before the \".\".",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "code",
            "text": "streams_xattr:prefix"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "code",
            "text": "streams_xattr:prefix"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0022",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "The overflow xattrs will be named according to a pattern following \"user.DosStreamExt.0.ADS-NAME\".",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0023",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "EXAMPLES",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0024",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "AUTHOR",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0025",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "The original Samba software and related utilities were created by Andrew Tridgell. Samba is now developed by the Samba Team as an Open Source project similar to the way the Linux kernel is developed.",
      "protected": []
    }
  ],
